@startuml class-judges
!include elvira.iuml
' What: one Panel per job asks narrow questions through process-lived clients; every answer is a Verdict with a band, or None (passed through unjudged).
' Kind: UML class diagram, specification level. Scope: evilflowers_worker.judges; the services that call it are left out.
' Source: issues evilflowers-worker#6, #10; evilflowers-knowledge Cookbooks/Deploy-Decision-Models, Cookbooks/Shared-Inference (2026-11-16)

title judges extra: questions, clients, panel (evilflowers-worker#6, #10, 2026-11-16)

package "evilflowers_worker.judges" {
  class Panel <<focus>> {
    budget : Budget
    ask(judge, question, state, images) : Verdict | None
    ask_batch(judge, question, states) : list[Verdict | None]
  }
  class Judges {
    decider : DeciderClient | None
    decider_vision : DeciderClient | None
    ollama : OllamaClient | None
    rerank : RerankClient | None
    from_settings(settings) : Judges
    panel() : Panel
  }
  class Budget {
    calls : int
    seconds : float
    allows() : bool
    spend(seconds)
  }
  class CircuitBreaker {
    failures : int
    reset : float
    allow() : bool
    success()
    failure()
  }
  interface Judge {
    name : str
    timeout : float
    breaker : CircuitBreaker
    batches : bool
    ask(question, state, images, timeout) : Verdict
    ask_batch(question, states, timeout) : list[Verdict | JudgeInvalid]
  }
  class DeciderClient {
    POST /v1/systemone
    POST /v1/systemone/batch (decider only, <= 64 states)
    vision : bool
  }
  class OllamaClient {
    POST /api/chat
  }
  class RerankClient {
    POST /rerank
  }
  class Choice {
    id : str
    instructions : str
    criteria : dict[str, str]
    reject : frozenset[str]
  }
  class Binary {
    id : str
    instructions : str
    reject : frozenset[str]
  }
  class Verdict {
    question : str
    verdict : str
    p : float
    reason : str | None
    model : str
    revision : str | None
    band : keep | review | hide | None
    region_fields() : dict
    paragraph_fields() : dict
  }
  class Thresholds {
    keep : float
    hide : float
    band(question, verdict) : Band
  }
  class JudgeSettings {
    judges_enabled, *_url, *_timeout
    judge_thresholds : dict[str, Thresholds]
    judge_budget_calls, judge_budget_seconds
  }
}

Judges *-- "0..4" Judge : process-lived clients
Judges ..> JudgeSettings : <<reads>>
Judges ..> Panel : <<creates>> one per job
Panel *-- Budget : per job
Panel ..> Judge : ask, ask_batch (64 states per request)
Panel ..> Thresholds : band from settings
Judge *-- CircuitBreaker : per client
Judge <|.. DeciderClient
Judge <|.. OllamaClient
Judge <|.. RerankClient
Judge ..> Choice : asks
Judge ..> Binary : asks
Judge ..> Verdict : answers

caption A Panel never raises for a model's failure: unreachable, open breaker, spent budget, refusal or an unparseable answer\nall return None and count <service>_judge_total{question,outcome,band}. Thresholds come from settings (knowledge#65).
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · evilflowers-worker · docs/diagrams/class-judges.puml
@enduml
